From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:47:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246:
 Add pmic-glink
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PM7250B that charges the battery and runs the Type-C port sits on
an SPMI bus the ADSP owns, so on this phone both are reached through
pmic-glink. Describe its one connector, USB 2.0 only, and let it set the
controller's role instead of fixing it to peripheral.

To be folded into the board commit once it has run.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
(cherry picked from commit 695c17fcc33c0d12ee608b7bb4c0524bb60c9976)
---
 .../sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts    | 38 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
index ed5dee79f..42293d5de 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
@@ -46,6 +46,38 @@ key-volume-down {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The charger and the Type-C port controller, a PM7250B, sit on an
+	 * SPMI bus the ADSP owns, so the port is reached through it. The
+	 * port is wired for USB 2.0 only.
+	 */
+	pmic-glink {
+		compatible = "qcom,sm6450-pmic-glink", "qcom,pmic-glink";
+
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		connector@0 {
+			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
+			reg = <0>;
+			power-role = "dual";
+			data-role = "dual";
+
+			ports {
+				#address-cells = <1>;
+				#size-cells = <0>;
+
+				port@0 {
+					reg = <0>;
+
+					pmic_glink_hs_in: endpoint {
+						remote-endpoint = <&usb_1_dwc3_hs>;
+					};
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * The panel's 1.8V logic supply is switched on by driving PM6150L
 	 * GPIO 9 low. With it the other way round the panel still takes
@@ -536,11 +568,13 @@ &ufs_mem_phy {
 };
 
 &usb_1 {
-	dr_mode = "peripheral";
-
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usb_1_dwc3_hs {
+	remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_hs_in>;
+};
+
 /*
  * The stock tree tunes this PHY with a raw register write,
  * qcom,param-override-seq, into HS_PHY_OVERRIDE_X0 through X3. Every field
